[8.025963, "i", "printf '%s\\n' '--- forms ---'; cat /app/opsfold/forms.txt; printf '%s\\n' '--- route ---'; cat /app/opsfold/ROUTE.txt; printf '%s\\n' '--- hull ---'; cat /app/opsfold/HULL.txt\n"]
[8.026601, "o", "printf '%s\\n' '--- forms ---'; cat /app/opsfold/forms.txt; printf '%s\\n' '--- route ---'; cat /app/opsfold/ROUTE.txt; printf '%s\\n' '--- hull ---'; cat /app/opsfold/HULL.txt\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[8.027048, "o", "--- forms ---\r\n"]
[8.028192, "o", "Change card lines:\r\n\r\n  BUDGET <integer>\r\n  ORIGIN <token>\r\n  FILE <path>\r\n  LINES <integers>\r\n  END\r\n\r\nCoverage count for a name is how many (FILE, line) pairs appear both on the change card and on that name's mesh sheet. Rank pool by that count, highest first. Equal counts: the lexicographically smaller identifier sits earlier.\r\n\r\nnames is the longest prefix of pool whose durations from /app/durcards/ticks.txt sum to at most BUDGET. spent_ms is that sum.\r\n\r\nslate.json is one object: keys pool, names, spent_ms in that order, no extra whitespace inside arrays besides JSON commas.\r\n\r\nslate.bin concatenates: four bytes SLT1, uint16be pool count, then that many records of uint16be length plus UTF-8 identifier, then uint16be names count and the same record shape, then uint32be spent_ms.\r\n"]
[8.028649, "o", "--- route ---\r\n"]
[8.029703, "o", "Pipeline modules:\r\n\r\n- /app/heapwell\r\n- /app/spanurn\r\n- /app/tickpit\r\n\r\nCLI lives under /app/cribcli. Emit lives under /app/emitkit.\r\n\r\n`--stable-order` reorders the loaded rows by coverage count. Ops turned it on when a budgeted prefix drifted; the counts on a single cull still matched.\r\n"]
[8.029961, "o", "--- hull ---\r\n"]
[8.03111, "o", "Throwaway mill: make -C /app/cribcli -f driver.mk OUT=/tmp/skiffloom.ref\r\nDesk rebuild: /app/kindle.sh\r\n"]
